<section id="s-imbalance" data-code="imbalance">
<div class="section-no">05 — Data Imbalance</div>
<h2>How Token Zipf Distribution Shapes Curvature</h2>
<p>Training data in LLM pretraining is highly long-tailed: some tokens are extremely frequent, while others are incredibly rare. By running controlled experiments on Zipf-imbalanced datasets with exponent <span class="math-var">s</span>, the researchers uncovered a key interaction: **data imbalance directly amplifies Muon's curvature advantage**.</p>
<p>Under uniform token frequencies (<span class="math-var">s = 0</span>), both optimizers incur moderate sharpness. But as imbalance increases to <span class="math-var">s = 1.0</span>, Adam's directional sharpness shoots up by 1.45× because its updates align strongly with high-frequency, high-curvature modes. Muon's spectrally normalized updates remain robustly balanced, widening the NDS gap by **1.8×**.</p>

