<section id="s-theory" data-code="theory">
<div class="section-no">06 — Energy Balancing Theory</div>
<h2>Theoretical Verification on Heterogeneous Contours</h2>
<p>To mathematically formalize these findings, the authors prove Theorem 5.5 on a stylized quadratic model with a two-group spectrum: a small group of high-curvature (sharp) modes <span class="math-var">w<sub>H</sub></span> and a large group of low-curvature (flat) modes <span class="math-var">w<sub>L</sub></span>.</p>
<p>The proof demonstrates that GD and Adam concentrate their update energy in the sharp modes because they inherit the gradient's alignment bias. Muon, by setting all singular values to 1, forces the update energy to be distributed **equally** across all active modes. This energy-balancing mechanism prevents Muon from overshooting the sharp modes and guarantees a smaller time-averaged NDS.</p>

